  "term": "Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination",
  "definition": "The Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination is a cognitive assessment used to help classify cognitive impairment, including cognitive impairment without dementia and dementia. In the supplied source, a revised version of this examination was used together with a functional scale in older adults.",
